    {
      "turn": 7,
      "doctor_question": "When you're managing your responsibilities — like keeping track of your schedule, organizing your gear, paying bills, or keeping your living space in order — do you find yourself struggling with that kind of stuff? Or does that come pretty naturally to you?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S009",
      "patient_response": "Um, well... I try really hard to keep everything organized. I really do. I don't want you to think my life is a total mess or anything, because I usually manage to get things done eventually! \n\nBut, um... I guess I do struggle a little bit with remembering the smaller details? It's just... I keep forgetting stuff that I honestly, truly mean to do. Like, I'll completely intend to sign off on my training modules at the station, or call people back, and it just... poof, it's gone from my brain. Or, um, sometimes I might not pay a bill until the late fee hits, which is really embarrassing to admit. Or I'll forget to bring the right gear paperwork in on shift.\n\nI always apologize to the captain when that happens, and I fix it right away! I really don't want to be a burden on anyone, and I know how important that paperwork is. I just... I don't know why those things slip past me when I'm trying so hard to keep track of them. I hope that doesn't make me sound completely irresponsible? I really am trying my best to stay on top of it all. Is it... is it normal to struggle with that kind of stuff even when you're really trying?",
      "new_confirmed_symptoms": [
